WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.033
Chespin, Chespin.

2
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.033
-Pin, pin, ches!

3
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.533
- We close to a Pokémon Center?
- Chespin.

4
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.133
We still have a ways to go.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.633
Just hang in there.

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.766
Pikachu.

7
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:26.000
Everything's starting to get hazy.

8
00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:28.500
Well, I'm feeling super-duper.

9
00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:30.166
Dedenne.

10
00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:34.500
I wish that I were Dedenne or Squishy.

11
00:00:34.966 --> 00:00:36.133
Yeah, me, too.

12
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.833
The sun is really, really hot, and the air is so dry.

13
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.300
I totally understand.

14
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:44.766
Isn't there anywhere we can take a rest for a while?

15
00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:46.766
It doesn't look like it.

16
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.133
I think I'm going to pass out.

17
00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:53.000
Pika!

18
00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:54.466
Huh?

19
00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:01.366
What's that?

20
00:01:02.966 --> 00:01:05.866
A robot, wow!

21
00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:14.566
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

22
00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:18.200
♪ Knock me down, I'll just get up again ♪

23
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:22.266
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

24
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:25.333
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

25
00:01:25.466 --> 00:01:26.500
♪ Gotta catch 'em all!

26
00:01:26.566 --> 00:01:29.900
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

27
00:01:29.966 --> 00:01:33.000
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

28
00:01:33.066 --> 00:01:34.533
♪ Gotta catch 'em all! ♪

29
00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:48.800
As our heroes journey to Snowbelle City,

30
00:01:48.866 --> 00:01:52.000
where Ash hopes to win his eighth Kalos Gym badge,

31
00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:56.633
they've discovered a robot digging in the middle of a scorching wasteland.

32
00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.566
What a retro-looking robot.

33
00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.966
It must've been built ages ago.

34
00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.566
It looks kind of beat-up.

35
00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:04.966
I wonder what it's doing way out here.

36
00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:05.866
Pikachu.

37
00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:09.900
Get out of the way.

38
00:02:09.966 --> 00:02:11.233
It talks.

39
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.866
Yes, I can speak.

40
00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.466
You've got AI.

41
00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:18.033
I never would've guessed from the way you look. Excellent.

42
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.333
Huh?

43
00:02:26.366 --> 00:02:29.133
Hmm. You know, those look like seeds.

44
00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.300
What are you doing?

45
00:02:33.066 --> 00:02:36.400
- Those are seeds. I'm planting them.
- Way out here?

46
00:02:36.966 --> 00:02:37.966
Huh?

47
00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.000
In this hot, dried-out place?

48
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.500
- Will they grow?
- I'm not sure.

49
00:02:42.566 --> 00:02:44.966
I wonder if it's been here a long time.

50
00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.000
It looks like quite a few years.

51
00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.833
Someone must've programmed it to do this work.

52
00:02:50.433 --> 00:02:51.966
- Pikachu!

53
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.433
What's that?

54
00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.433
A Pokémon?

55
00:02:57.066 --> 00:02:58.200
What kind?

56
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.066
Chesnaught.

57
00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:03.600
The Spiny Armor Pokémon, and the final evolved form of Chespin.

58
00:03:03.766 --> 00:03:07.700
Its tackle is so powerful, it can overturn a 50-ton tank.

59
00:03:07.766 --> 00:03:09.333
That's a lot of power.

60
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.166
And it's coming right for us.

61
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.466
- Wow.
- Admire it later.

62
00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:26.333
- I think we'd better retreat.
- Yeah.

63
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.200
- Why did we all get attacked like that?
- Chesnaught's protecting the robot.

64
00:03:35.266 --> 00:03:38.066
- Maybe they're really good friends.
- Could be.

65
00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.633
- Ches!
- Huh?

66
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.733
Chespin, Chespin.

67
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:45.933
What's this?

68
00:03:46.266 --> 00:03:49.033
Perhaps it has something to do with the robot.

69
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.300
There's no one here.

70
00:03:50.366 --> 00:03:51.366
Amazing.

71
00:03:51.633 --> 00:03:54.033
Looks like some kind of research lab.

72
00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.466
This place has something to do with those two.

73
00:03:59.933 --> 00:04:02.766
They must've been cultivating plants in here.

74
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:04.133
Uh, look.

75
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.066
Who's that?

76
00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:10.600
Hey, what are you doing?

77
00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.500
- Huh?
- Pika?

78
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:17.500
Oh, hi there. My name is Ash, and this is my partner, Pikachu.

79
00:04:17.566 --> 00:04:19.000
Pika. Pikachu.

80
00:04:19.066 --> 00:04:20.333
Hi. I'm Serena.

81
00:04:20.399 --> 00:04:21.300
I'm Bonnie.

82
00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.466
This is Dedenne and Squishy.

83
00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:25.166
Dedenne.

84
00:04:25.233 --> 00:04:26.566
That's my big brother.

85
00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.800
My name is Clemont.

86
00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:29.033
Chespin. Ches!

87
00:04:29.466 --> 00:04:32.033
What do you want with the Chapman Research Lab?

88
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.300
We're interested in a robot we saw outside.

89
00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:37.800
So, who are you?

90
00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:39.100
May name is Henny.

91
00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:42.000
That man in the photograph is my grandfather.

92
00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:46.533
You wanna know about Robon, watch this.

93
00:04:47.566 --> 00:04:49.133
My name is Chapman.

94
00:04:49.633 --> 00:04:52.200
I'm a scientist researching environments

95
00:04:52.266 --> 00:04:55.333
where people and Pokémon can live together happily.

96
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.666
You see, once upon a time,

97
00:04:57.733 --> 00:05:00.966
this beautiful forest was nature at its finest,

98
00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.466
filled with many wild Pokémon.

99
00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:07.933
But one day, the forest began to dry up and wither.

100
00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.333
I did my best to figure out the reason why,

101
00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:16.233
but my work was unfortunately cut short by an unexpected illness.

102
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:21.600
I was able to construct Robon to help the forest regrow,

103
00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.366
but I'm afraid I won't be around to see it come to fruition.

104
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.766
The forest is now dried-up.

105
00:05:30.066 --> 00:05:32.866
Neither people nor Pokémon can live here.

106
00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:38.633
Its only remaining hope is with my robot, Robon, and Chesnaught.

107
00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:43.700
If they somehow encounter difficulties, I would like you to help them.

108
00:05:44.533 --> 00:05:48.900
I ask this of whoever is watching this as my final request.

109
00:05:51.366 --> 00:05:56.466
Chesnaught attacked us because it thought we were interfering with Robon's work.

110
00:05:56.533 --> 00:06:01.333
Even though Grandfather's gone, Robon keeps on planting seeds

111
00:06:01.466 --> 00:06:04.000
and Chesnaught keeps on protecting Robon.

112
00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.066
- Huh?

113
00:06:09.633 --> 00:06:10.466
Robon.

114
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.900
Huh?

115
00:06:20.733 --> 00:06:23.400
- Robon can even charge itself?
- Yeah.

116
00:06:23.866 --> 00:06:26.733
But lately that's been taking longer and longer.

117
00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:31.300
I think it's working way too hard and must be starting to break down.

118
00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.766
Let me have a look.

119
00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.133
Huh?

120
00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:38.900
Hmm.

121
00:06:38.966 --> 00:06:40.833
I'm certain I can fix this.

122
00:06:41.633 --> 00:06:43.766
My big brother's an inventor.

123
00:06:43.833 --> 00:06:45.500
He can fix any machine.

124
00:06:45.566 --> 00:06:46.733
- Stop it!
- Huh?

125
00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.066
What I really want is for Robon and Chesnaught to stop working so hard.

126
00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:54.433
They've worked hard enough already.

127
00:06:56.566 --> 00:06:59.800
But you know Robon's mission is to replant the forest.

128
00:07:00.333 --> 00:07:02.966
Instead of stopping Robon, we should help it

129
00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:06.033
accomplish the very reason why it was constructed.

130
00:07:06.466 --> 00:07:09.333
But it's been working so hard, with no progress.

131
00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.800
- It's impossible.
- The progress of science stops cold

132
00:07:12.866 --> 00:07:14.366
the moment you give up.

133
00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:17.833
Continuing no matter what challenges appear is key

134
00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.733
to making scientific progress.

135
00:07:20.166 --> 00:07:21.000
Chespin.

136
00:07:21.466 --> 00:07:22.566
Clemont's right.

137
00:07:22.633 --> 00:07:23.933
I think so, too.

138
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.266
Taking on challenges is the only way.

139
00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.600
Pikachu.

140
00:07:31.666 --> 00:07:32.633
I hear you.

141
00:07:33.933 --> 00:07:36.266
- I'll do whatever I can.
- That's great.

142
00:07:39.566 --> 00:07:40.700
Charge complete.

143
00:07:41.266 --> 00:07:43.266
It charged way faster this time.

144
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.233
Thank you so much, Clemont.

145
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.500
So, now we know what we've gotta do.

146
00:07:53.066 --> 00:07:55.866
This whole area is so enormous.

147
00:07:55.933 --> 00:07:57.533
- Huh?

148
00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.566
- Chesnaught.
- Stop, Chesnaught.

149
00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.500
Everybody just really wants to help Robon out.

150
00:08:03.966 --> 00:08:04.933
Pikachu.

151
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.066
Pin, pin, ches!

152
00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:08.066
You've gotta trust us, Chesnaught.

153
00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:09.033
Ches, pin, pin!

154
00:08:10.233 --> 00:08:11.233
Hmm...

155
00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.533
Chesnaught.

156
00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.166
I think it understands.

157
00:08:18.233 --> 00:08:20.233
- Pika!
- Thank you, Chesnaught.

158
00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.900
Let's get this forest back in shape.

159
00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.800
- Yeah.
- Pika!

160
00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:30.166
First off, we need to figure out whether or not plants can even grow here.

161
00:08:30.233 --> 00:08:32.000
So, how are we gonna do that?

162
00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.466
The future is now, thanks to science.

163
00:08:35.933 --> 00:08:37.299
Clemontic Gear, on.

164
00:08:37.766 --> 00:08:41.433
I thought we'd encounter a situation precisely like this one.

165
00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.833
I call it the Mr. Dirt Analyzing Simulator.

166
00:08:44.933 --> 00:08:46.566
I like that name, Clemont.

167
00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.033
All right, then, here we go.

168
00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:53.066
Beginning analysis.

169
00:08:56.633 --> 00:08:59.500
It's a device that analyze the soil's components

170
00:08:59.566 --> 00:09:02.766
and determine whether or not seeds are able to grow.

171
00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:12.533
Growth in this soil is impossible.

172
00:09:13.166 --> 00:09:18.100
- Looks like this isn't going to work out.
- So, Clemont, what are we gonna do?

173
00:09:18.166 --> 00:09:19.933
If this was once a forest,

174
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.866
there must be underground water somewhere here.

175
00:09:22.933 --> 00:09:24.733
Let's figure out where.

176
00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.600
Lux.

177
00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:29.566
All right, I choose you.

178
00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.100
Noi.

179
00:09:32.166 --> 00:09:33.966
Use your special eyesight.

180
00:09:34.033 --> 00:09:36.000
Noibat will use its supersonic.

181
00:09:36.066 --> 00:09:39.266
- Search for an underground water source.
- Do it, too.

182
00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.200
- Ray... lux!
- Noibat.

183
00:09:44.433 --> 00:09:45.400
Hmm?

184
00:09:45.466 --> 00:09:47.633
- Ches, ches, ches!
- Huh?

185
00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.266
Chespin's putting its vines into the ground

186
00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:53.400
to search for water, too. That's an excellent idea.

187
00:09:57.033 --> 00:09:59.900
It's great that you wanna help, too, Chesnaught.

188
00:10:07.066 --> 00:10:11.100
Looks like the twerps are up to some weird-looking stuff, as usual.

189
00:10:11.166 --> 00:10:12.733
What a big, fat bore.

190
00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.433
Instead, we should all focus on catching that power-packed Chesnaught.

191
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.533
That addition would give us a potent power punch.

192
00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:21.933
Wobbuffet!

193
00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.966
- Chespin.
- Chesnaught.

194
00:10:29.433 --> 00:10:32.533
- Chespin, ches.
- Ches, Chesnaught, naught.

195
00:10:38.533 --> 00:10:40.266
Ches! Chesnaught, naught.

196
00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.600
Chespin, Chespin.

197
00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.333
Pin, pin, Chespin.

198
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.233
Luxray, ray.

199
00:10:57.566 --> 00:11:00.966
All right, Chespin and Chesnaught. Way to go. Great.

200
00:11:01.033 --> 00:11:02.766
Thanks, Noibat. Return.

201
00:11:04.133 --> 00:11:06.733
- Nice work, Chesnaught.
- Chesnaught.

202
00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:08.033
Now it's your turn.

203
00:11:10.533 --> 00:11:11.933
Bunnelby, use dig.

204
00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.266
Bunnelby!

205
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.233
Yeah. Come on.

206
00:11:25.366 --> 00:11:26.566
What's up, Bunnelby?

207
00:11:26.633 --> 00:11:27.633
Bun.

208
00:11:29.933 --> 00:11:33.133
- What's this?
- It looks like we may have hit bedrock.

209
00:11:34.266 --> 00:11:35.866
Time to investigate.

210
00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.900
It's huge. Ten meters in diameter.

211
00:11:39.966 --> 00:11:43.900
The water's below. We can't get to it, unless we move the rock.

212
00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.600
Pika.

213
00:11:47.966 --> 00:11:50.100
Who's that Pokémon?

214
00:11:54.966 --> 00:11:56.700
It's Chesnaught!

215
00:11:56.833 --> 00:11:58.766
Chesnaught.

216
00:12:01.566 --> 00:12:05.966
Seismic activities shifted the rock until it formed kind of a lid.

217
00:12:06.033 --> 00:12:08.933
Question is, how will we get it out of the way?

218
00:12:09.533 --> 00:12:11.700
- Ches!
- Chesnaught, naught, ches.

219
00:12:11.766 --> 00:12:14.200
Chespin!

220
00:12:14.266 --> 00:12:17.166
Chesnaught!

221
00:12:22.633 --> 00:12:25.533
- No good.
- So, in order to break the rock,

222
00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:28.533
we need to heat it up, then rapidly cool it down.

223
00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.600
We'll all have to attack at once.

224
00:12:30.666 --> 00:12:32.133
- Let's do it.
- All right.

225
00:12:35.633 --> 00:12:37.400
Now, Braixen, flamethrower.

226
00:12:37.466 --> 00:12:38.900
Braixen!

227
00:12:42.433 --> 00:12:44.033
Greninja, water shuriken.

228
00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.900
Greninja.

229
00:12:47.433 --> 00:12:49.000
Chespin, use pin missile.

230
00:12:49.066 --> 00:12:50.466
Bunnelby, use mud shot.

231
00:12:50.533 --> 00:12:52.266
And Luxray, use swift. Now.

232
00:12:52.333 --> 00:12:54.233
Pikachu, electro ball.

233
00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.100
Sylveon, swift, let's go.

234
00:12:56.166 --> 00:12:57.300
Chespin!

235
00:12:57.366 --> 00:12:58.733
Bunnelby!

236
00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.666
Luxray!

237
00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.600
Chesnaught!

238
00:13:07.866 --> 00:13:09.033
So, how did we do?

239
00:13:10.366 --> 00:13:11.566
No way.

240
00:13:12.433 --> 00:13:14.133
Anything else we can do?

241
00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:17.800
Let's see. If we can't break it, maybe we could pull it out.

242
00:13:19.833 --> 00:13:21.200
Let's pull hard.

243
00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:24.933
We'll call it the "if you can't break it, pull it" strategy.

244
00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:26.966
There's no science in that name.

245
00:13:27.033 --> 00:13:29.300
- Okay, then let's do it.
- All right.

246
00:13:29.766 --> 00:13:31.833
- Pikachu.
- Chespin, pin.

247
00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.300
- Okay, on three.
- Right!

248
00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.866
And one, two, three.

249
00:13:43.666 --> 00:13:44.966
Pikachu!

250
00:13:45.033 --> 00:13:46.433
Hey, what's going on?

251
00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:49.433
Prepare for trouble. We're going on.

252
00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.633
And make it double, from dawn to dawn.

253
00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:56.500
- To protect the world from devastation.
- To unite all people within our nation.

254
00:13:56.566 --> 00:13:59.333
We're ignoring this dry, barren land.

255
00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.233
Extending our reach for the treasures at hand.

256
00:14:03.033 --> 00:14:04.800
- Jesse.
- And James.

257
00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:08.600
Team Rocket stays calm while you twerps lose your cool.

258
00:14:08.666 --> 00:14:11.166
Surrender now or fight, that's the rule.

259
00:14:11.233 --> 00:14:12.733
Meowth's no fool. Yeah!

260
00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.333
Wobbuffet!

261
00:14:16.066 --> 00:14:18.533
- Team Rocket.
- What do you want?

262
00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.700
- What?
- Not what, but who.

263
00:14:20.766 --> 00:14:23.333
Thought we'd grab Chesnaught. Pikachu, too.

264
00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.200
Then we thought, why not grab all of them, too?

265
00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:28.766
Wobbuff--

266
00:14:30.033 --> 00:14:31.600
Get out of the way.

267
00:14:31.666 --> 00:14:32.933
What's with that?

268
00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.766
There are seeds planted here.

269
00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:36.266
Please, move away.

270
00:14:36.333 --> 00:14:37.333
Seeds, huh?

271
00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:38.500
Robon...

272
00:14:38.566 --> 00:14:40.100
Please, move away.

273
00:14:40.366 --> 00:14:42.533
How annoying. Gourgeist, come.

274
00:14:43.966 --> 00:14:44.933
Gourgeist.

275
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.633
Quiet that tin can down.

276
00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:47.533
Gourgeist!

277
00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:48.833
Uh-oh!

278
00:14:49.333 --> 00:14:50.266
Chesnaught!

279
00:14:52.533 --> 00:14:53.833
Cover those teeth.

280
00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:57.500
Those super-reinforced lassos will keep you chumps in place.

281
00:14:58.266 --> 00:15:01.600
Chesnaught!

282
00:15:03.433 --> 00:15:07.166
Chesnaught. No. No.

283
00:15:10.933 --> 00:15:15.033
Perfect. Now, I want you two to always help each other out.

284
00:15:15.533 --> 00:15:18.200
Always care for each other, no matter what.

285
00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.100
Chesnaught!

286
00:15:20.166 --> 00:15:24.100
The two of you are this land's only hope of survival.

287
00:15:24.166 --> 00:15:26.833
Do me a favor, Gourgeist, calm Chesnaught.

288
00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.900
Inkay. Psybeam, go.

289
00:15:35.466 --> 00:15:37.666
Chesnaught and I are its only hope.

290
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.066
Hope, hope, hope.

291
00:15:46.666 --> 00:15:48.266
Oh, Robon, please, get up.

292
00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:18.900
- Okay, now you're gonna get it.
- Rain check, please!

293
00:16:18.966 --> 00:16:21.133
Greninja, use water shuriken. Now.

294
00:16:21.633 --> 00:16:23.933
- Pikachu, thunderbolt.
- Greninja.

295
00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.366
Now, Braixen, fire blast.

296
00:16:26.766 --> 00:16:29.833
Chespin, pin missile. And Luxray, use swift.

297
00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.800
- Chespin!
- Luxray!

298
00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.133
We're blasting off again!

299
00:16:43.133 --> 00:16:44.200
Robon.

300
00:16:45.333 --> 00:16:46.700
No, Robon.

301
00:16:51.633 --> 00:16:54.566
- Ches.
- Pin, pin, ches.

302
00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:56.100
Uh-oh.

303
00:16:56.166 --> 00:16:58.166
- Robon's broken.
- Yeah.

304
00:16:58.233 --> 00:16:59.066
Pika.

305
00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.733
Progress of science stops the moment you give up.

306
00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:08.366
If you don't give up, anything is possible.

307
00:17:34.966 --> 00:17:36.600
Robon's as good as new.

308
00:17:38.733 --> 00:17:40.733
Reboot. Reset.

309
00:17:41.833 --> 00:17:44.266
Reset complete, and Robon feels great.

310
00:17:44.433 --> 00:17:48.400
- You're back, Robon. You're really back.
- Chesnaught, Chesnaught.

311
00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:55.600
Robon? What do we do about that rock?

312
00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:01.133
Obstacle present. Scanning.

313
00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:10.033
Rock removal operation commencing.

314
00:18:10.766 --> 00:18:12.633
I will now remove the rock.

315
00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.266
I didn't know Robon can do that.

316
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.166
Go, Robon!

317
00:18:26.233 --> 00:18:27.566
Show us how it's done!

318
00:18:27.633 --> 00:18:28.966
Do it!

319
00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:35.333
It's a gusher!

320
00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.866
The spring is flowing again.

321
00:18:38.933 --> 00:18:39.800
All right!

322
00:18:40.266 --> 00:18:43.300
- Chesnaught! Chesnaught!
- Chespin!

323
00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:58.700
Oh, wow, it's beautiful. Look at the water, Dedenne and Squishy.

324
00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:06.233
Why don't we analyze the soil once again?

325
00:19:08.033 --> 00:19:09.900
Beginning analysis.

326
00:19:21.333 --> 00:19:24.366
Growth in this soil is very possible.

327
00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.700
Now Grandfather's dream will come true.

328
00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.266
I realized when I was fixing Robon

329
00:19:36.333 --> 00:19:40.000
that each one of its parts was constructed with lots of love.

330
00:19:40.066 --> 00:19:42.966
Professor Chapman was a great inventor indeed.

331
00:19:43.266 --> 00:19:45.100
And I wanna be just like him.

332
00:19:45.166 --> 00:19:46.700
Chespin.

333
00:19:48.066 --> 00:19:52.666
Clemont, I've decided I'm going to pursue the path of science just like you.

334
00:19:53.066 --> 00:19:57.333
Then if Robon ever needs fixing again, I'll be able to do it.

335
00:19:58.066 --> 00:20:00.833
Great. And I know you will do it, too.

336
00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.733
- Lots of luck to you, Henny.
- Thank you, Clemont.

337
00:20:05.433 --> 00:20:08.866
- Naught, ches, Chesnaught, ches.
- Chespin, Chespin, pin.

338
00:20:10.666 --> 00:20:12.000
- Bye-bye.
- Bye.

339
00:20:12.066 --> 00:20:13.200
Pika, pika!

340
00:20:15.066 --> 00:20:17.266
- Goodbye, everyone.
- Chesnaught, Chesnaught.

341
00:20:17.333 --> 00:20:20.666
- Take good care.
- See you again. I know it.

342
00:20:22.933 --> 00:20:25.066
And so, with everyone's help,

343
00:20:25.133 --> 00:20:27.933
a water source was discovered and unleashed,

344
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.433
and water now gushes powerfully through the parched land.

345
00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:34.566
And our heroes are off again to Snowbelle City...

346
00:20:43.966 --> 00:20:46.466
as the journey continues.
